# s20-large-group authoring scratch: turns, part 2 (floor, invoicing, pains and cost, departures, upside, install).

TURNS2 = [
    ("Con", "Rosalind, the floor."),
    ("Ros", "The floor gets a job ticket. Lettie prints it off the job sheet, one ticket per job, and it goes in a plastic sleeve on the floor board. The floor board is a whiteboard, twelve feet of it, columns for print, cut, fab, paint, assembly, ready. The ticket moves along the board as the job moves. That's the system, and honestly it works better than anything on a screen has ever worked for us.", "ros_floorboard"),
    ("Con", "What's on the ticket?"),
    ("Ros", "Whatever was in the job sheet when Lettie printed it. Sizes, quantities, material, finish, due date. Not the proof. The proof's a separate print-out if someone remembers to attach it, and it might be the wrong version, which is how we got nineteen backwards arrows."),
    ("Con", "What does ready mean on the board?"),
    ("Ros", "Ready means it's in the ready column. Which means someone moved it there. Which usually means it's ready. Usually.", "ros_ready"),
    ("Del", "Usually is the word doing all the work in that sentence."),
    ("Con", "And if the job sheet changes after the ticket's printed?"),
    ("Ros", "Then the ticket's wrong and nobody knows. That's Quarrington in one sentence. That's most of our remakes in one sentence.", "ros_stale_ticket"),
    ("Kwa", "Can I add to that, because that's mine. A customer changes the copy on a panel after sign-off. Happens every week. I tell Henrike by email. Whether that reaches the floor before the panel's cut is a coin flip, and I'm not exaggerating, it's about half.", "kwa_changeorder"),
    ("Hen", "It's not half."),
    ("Kwa", "It's a lot.", "kwa_withdraws"),
    ("Hen", "It's a lot. It's not half.", "hen_not_half"),
    ("Con", "What do you call that, a customer changing something after sign-off?"),
    ("Kwa", "A change order. If it's big enough to charge for. If it's small we just do it, which is its own problem.", "kwa_co_def"),
    ("Con", "Okay. Delphine, is install next, or does something happen between the floor and the van?"),
    ("Del", "Install is next. Calum will tell you install is where it all lands, because he gets the job last and he gets it with whatever's gone wrong upstream.", "del_calum_defer"),
    ("Con", "We'll come to install. Bronwyn, I promised you early. Where does finance touch a job?", "con_install_deferred"),
    ("Bro", "Twice. I open it and give it a number at the start, we've covered that. And I invoice it at the end, when I know it's installed. And there's the problem. I don't know it's installed. Nobody tells finance a job is on the wall. I find out because a coordinator mentions it, or a customer rings about something else, or I walk the floor on a Friday and ask.", "bro_p4_stated"),
    ("Con", "How late does that make the invoice?", "con_p4_concrete_q"),
    ("Bro", "I pulled it before this call. Average from install to invoice, forty-one days. Forty-one. For work we've already done and already paid the crew for.", "bro_p4_concrete"),
    ("Con", "Who feels that?", "con_p4_reach_q"),
    ("Bro", "Me, and the line of credit. There's about a million two sitting installed and not invoiced at any moment. Gideon feels it when I show him the cash position, which is why he's here, I imagine.", "bro_p4_reach"),
    ("Con", "And the Friday walk is the workaround. What stops you carrying on that way?", "con_p4_workaround_q"),
    ("Bro", "It doesn't scale. I can walk the Saginaw floor. I can't walk Flint, and I certainly can't walk a hundred and forty pharmacies.", "bro_p4_workaround"),
    ("Yol", "Can I say how Flint does it, since it's come up twice. We keep our own copy of the job sheet. The Saginaw one is unusable by Wednesday, there are two hundred rows and half the filters are somebody's leftovers. So we have the Flint sheet, twelve of us, one crew, and it's clean. And Bronwyn finds out we've installed something when I email her, which I do, mostly.", "yol_own_sheet"),
    ("Bro", "Mostly."),
    ("Yol", "Mostly."),
    ("Con", "So there are two job sheets."),
    ("Del", "There are two job sheets and one truth, and they're not the same thing. Yes."),
    ("Kwa", "Can I ask a boring one before I forget? If everyone who touches a job needs a login, that's the crews, that's the floor. Are we going to end up paying per head for people who'd open it twice a month?", "kwa_seat_question"),
    ("Con", "It depends on the plan and on how it's set up, and I'd rather answer that properly than off the top of my head. I'll put it in the recap with a straight answer.", "con_deferred_seats"),
    ("Kwa", "Fine. As long as someone answers it."),
    ("Con", "Let me pause the walk there, because I want to go back over the pieces that hurt and put some weight on them. Henrike, the retyping. You said twenty minutes to an hour per job, and then the chasing. Across the six of you, roughly how many hours a week go into retyping and chasing?", "con_p1_cost_q"),
    ("Hen", "Retyping alone, maybe two hours a week each. The chasing is the rest of it. If I'm honest, six hours a week each on things that only exist because the quote and the ticket and the proof don't talk to each other. Six each, and there are six of us.", "hen_hours"),
    ("Con", "Six hours a week, six people. Does that feel right to the room?"),
    ("Del", "It feels light, but it's Henrike's number and she'd know."),
    ("Con", "Bronwyn, while you're here. A coordinator, loaded, what do you carry them at?"),
    ("Bro", "Thirty-eight an hour loaded, give or take. Production leads are fifty-two. I'm not giving you the crew rate off the top of my head, it's a different structure with the overtime.", "bro_rates"),
    ("Con", "Understood. Rosalind, the floor side of the same problem. When a ticket's wrong or a proof's missing, what does it cost you in time, not materials, time?"),
    ("Ros", "My two leads. Call it eight hours a week between the two of them standing at the board with a ticket in one hand and a phone in the other, waiting for someone to tell them what the job actually is. Eight hours a week, easily. And that's the leads, not the people behind them who are also waiting.", "ros_wait_hours"),
    ("Con", "And today, how do you stop a wrong ticket getting to the floor?", "con_p1_workaround_q"),
    ("Hen", "We ring. A coordinator rings the floor and reads the ticket back against the quote, on the big ones. On the small ones we don't, there isn't time, and the small ones are where it goes wrong.", "hen_p1_workaround"),
    ("Con", "What stops you carrying on with the read-back?"),
    ("Hen", "A hundred and forty stores. I can't read a hundred and forty tickets down the phone. And it depends on who's in. When I'm off, nobody reads anything back.", "hen_p1_why_not"),
    ("Con", "Who else ends up dealing with a wrong ticket?", "con_p1_reach_q"),
    ("Ros", "My leads, who wait. Calum's crew, who go back out. Kwame, who explains it to the customer. And Bronwyn, who writes it off. It's everybody. That's the point Delphine made at the start.", "ros_p1_reach"),
    ("Con", "And the materials. Remakes. How often does a job get remade?", "con_remake_q"),
    ("Fer", "Honestly? One in ten. One in ten jobs has something remade. At our volume that's just a cost of doing business, and I say that as the person who has to explain it to the customer.", "fer_remake_rate"),
    ("Con", "One in ten."),
    ("Kwa", "That's about what I'd have said."),
    ("Con", "And what does a remake actually involve? Walk me through one."),
    ("Ros", "Depends on the panel. A vinyl panel, you reprint it, it's an hour and some material. A routed aluminium panel like Quarrington, it's a new blank, a day on the router, paint, cure, and the crew going back out. So a remake is anything from an hour to three days."),
    ("Con", "And the one-in-ten, does that match what you see?"),
    ("Ros", "No. It is not one in ten. From where I stand it's closer to one in four. One in four jobs has at least one panel go through the shop twice. I would put money on that.", "ros_remake_rate"),
    ("Fer", "[crosstalk] That's not -- that can't be right, we'd be --", "fer_crosstalk"),
    ("Ros", "[crosstalk] It depends whether you count the ones we catch before they ship.", "ros_crosstalk"),
    ("Con", "So one in ten and one in four. Which is it?", "con_which_is_it"),
    ("Fer", "Depends what you count. I count what the customer sees."),
    ("Ros", "And I count what the shop builds twice."),
    ("Del", "We've never measured it. That's the honest answer. Rosalind, you keep the remake log, can you pull it for the last quarter?", "del_never_measured"),
    ("Ros", "I can pull it. It's a paper book by the router, but I can count it. Give me a week."),
    ("Con", "Then I'll write down both numbers and neither of them, if that makes sense, until the book says. Bronwyn, is there a money figure on remakes?", "con_both_numbers"),
    ("Bro", "There's a budget line. We budget ninety a year for remake materials, that's materials only. Last year we actually wrote off, I want to say fifty-five. Fifty-five, fifty-six, on remake materials. That's the actual, and it's materials, it doesn't have the hours in it.", "bro_writeoff"),
    ("Con", "So the ninety is the budget and the fifty-five is what happened."),
    ("Bro", "Correct. Don't add them together, they're not the same thing."),
    ("Con", "I won't. Let me do the arithmetic out loud and you stop me. Coordinators, six people at six hours a week, thirty-six hours, at thirty-eight an hour, times fifty-two.", "con_arith"),
    ("Del", "Thirty-six times thirty-eight is... thirteen sixty-eight a week. Times fifty-two. Seventy-one thousand and change.", "del_math_coord"),
    ("Con", "Production leads, eight hours at fifty-two."),
    ("Del", "Four-sixteen a week. Times fifty-two. Twenty-one, twenty-two thousand.", "del_math_leads"),
    ("Con", "And the remake materials, the actual, fifty-five."),
    ("Del", "So seventy-one, plus twenty-two, plus fifty-five. A hundred and forty-eight thousand, near enough. A year. And that's without the remake hours, which nobody's counted, and without the install side, which we haven't got to.", "del_bleed_total"),
    ("Con", "A hundred and forty-eight thousand a year, without remake labour and without install. Bronwyn, does that feel right?"),
    ("Bro", "That's about right, and it's light. The remake hours would be the biggest number in there if we had it.", "bro_bleed_confirm"),
    ("Con", "Understood. I'll carry it as light."),
    ("Del", "Bronwyn, before you go, the audit. Say it so it's said."),
    ("Bro", "Nothing touches the accounting system before November. We're mid-audit until the end of the month and I'm not opening a connection to anything while they're in the building. After November, talk to me.", "bro_audit"),
    ("Con", "After November. Understood."),
    ("Bro", "That's me, I'm afraid. Auditors. Send me the list of what you need and I'll get you the numbers by end of week, the write-off figure properly and whatever else.", "bro_leaves"),
    ("Con", "Thank you, Bronwyn. I will."),
    ("Del", "Go. We'll manage."),
    ("Con", "Let me turn it round. If the retyping and the chasing went away, the thirty-six hours a week, what would the coordinators do with it?", "con_upside_q"),
    ("Hen", "Answer the phone. Half of what comes in is customers asking where their job is, and we can't tell them without ringing the floor.", "hen_upside"),
    ("Fer", "From my side, we'd quote faster. There's a lag between winning and the proof going out, and we lose jobs in that lag. Maybe two a month, I'd guess, maybe, where the customer gets bored and goes to someone quicker. I couldn't put a value on that, it's a guess.", "fer_upside_hedge"),
    ("Con", "Two a month, and you'd call that a guess. Fine, I'll carry it as one. Delphine, is there something you'd go after if the building could take it?"),
    ("Del", "The hospital framework. There's a regional health system that tenders its signage on a five-year framework, and we've not bid, because I can't show them how we'd run forty sites at once. That's the one. I'm not putting a number on it either.", "del_upside_target"),
    ("Con", "Understood. Before we go to what solved looks like, let me stop and ask the room something. Is there a part of how a job moves through this building that hasn't come up yet? Anyone. I'm happy with silence.", "con_open_checkin"),
    ("Con", "Take your time."),
    ("Cal", "Install.", "cal_first"),
    ("Con", "Calum. Go on."),
    ("Cal", "Install's where it lands, like Delphine said. I've got six crews, two people each, five here and Yolanda's one. I schedule them on a spreadsheet, a week at a time. And the thing nobody's said is that a crew turns up to a site and the job isn't ready. The sign's still in paint, or the permit's not through, or the site's not ready for us, and two people have driven two hours for nothing.", "cal_p3_stated"),
    ("Con", "When did that last happen?", "con_concrete_q"),
    ("Cal", "Traverse City, three weeks ago. Retail unit, four panels. The ticket said ready. The board said ready. One panel was in paint because it had been remade, and nobody moved the ticket back. Crew drove up, hung three, drove home, drove up again the following Tuesday for one panel.", "cal_p3_concrete"),
    ("Con", "How do you try to stop that today?"),
    ("Cal", "I ring the floor every morning. I walk it if I'm in. I ring Yolanda for hers. And I ring the site the day before, if I remember, and I don't always remember because I've got six crews and one of me.", "cal_p3_workaround"),
    ("Con", "And what stops you carrying on ringing?", "con_p3_workaround_q"),
    ("Cal", "The rollout. Eight crews on the road instead of six, if we hire, in five states. I can't ring five states every morning. I can barely ring Flint.", "cal_p3_trajectory"),
    ("Con", "Who else feels a wasted trip?", "con_p3_reach_q"),
    ("Cal", "The crew, because it's overtime nobody planned. The customer, because we've turned up twice. And the next job, because that crew was supposed to be somewhere else the day they go back.", "cal_p3_reach"),
    ("Con", "How often does a wasted trip happen?", "con_p3_cost_q"),
    ("Cal", "Two a month. Some months three. Call it two. Four hours each, two people, so sixteen hours a month of crew time, before the fuel.", "cal_p3_cost"),
    ("Con", "Sixteen hours a month. And the crew rate, is that something you carry?", "con_crew_rate_q"),
    ("Cal", "No. That's a Bronwyn number."),
    ("Del", "That's a Bronwyn number and she's gone. Put it on her list.", "del_crew_rate_gone"),
    ("Con", "On her list. Thank you, Calum, that's exactly the thing I was hoping someone would say."),
]
